This is a crypto scalping signal dashboard in Python.
- Use Streamlit for UI, Plotly for charts, ccxt for exchanges, the `ta` library for indicators.
- Binance USDT-M futures = data source (public data, no API key). MEXC futures = trade execution (much later).
- Keep code modular: one responsibility per file, following the project folder structure.
- Never hardcode API keys; read from .env using python-dotenv. Never print or log keys.
- Always include trading fees and slippage in any profit calculation.
- Never use future candles when calculating signals (no look-ahead bias).
- Add clear comments; the owner is not an expert programmer.
- Handle API and network errors gracefully; the dashboard must never crash.
- Always run commands inside the venv (Python 3.13).
- Entry file is streamlit_app.py (not app.py — Vercel reserves that name for Python serverless).
- Deploy the dashboard on Streamlit Community Cloud; Vercel is only a static landing page.
- Only build what is asked in the current prompt; do not jump ahead to later phases.